#question(title: [Another sequence defined by recurrence])[
  Consider the sequence
  $display({a_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ defined by
  $
    cases( & quad a_0 = 1, forall n in NN comma quad & quad a_(n + 1) = 1 - a_n)
  $

  - Use the same method as in the previous
    slide to compute its limit.
  - #strong[After] you have computed the
    limit, calculate $a_1$, $a_2$, $a_3$, and
    $a_4$.
  - What happened?
]
